Z||000002||Sootah||09-30-2001||08:14 PM||||1st, foremost, and easiest, K&N Filter.<P>2nd, remove the cat and replace it w/ a pipe or high flow replacement unit. (Depending on your states emmisions laws, we dont have testing here in southern Utah.. Moua ha ha haaa)<P>3rd, not a damn clue, I don't know crap bout engines.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">  <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||3
Z||000003||GTFiero1||09-30-2001||08:38 PM||||check this out. <A HREF="http://www.tornadofuelsaver.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tornadofuelsaver.com</A>   . this thing puts a spin on the air entering the engine so it winds around curves and such giveinf MORE HORSE POWER. I dont have a fiero yet but i know someone who put one of these in the 87 coupe with the Tech4 and he said that he felt the difference instantly.<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||10
Z||000004||artherd||10-01-2001||08:53 AM||||Pull one out of a GTO (and I don't mean a Pontiac GTO! ;)<P>I will leave it as an excercise to the reader to determine which automobiles in the US contained both the letters "GTO" in their name, and a 2.8litre engine under their skin.<P>(and wether said engine would indeed 'cook some rice' :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>Oh, K&N filter, and new cat will do good things for you.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||XDrewX||10-01-2001||12:22 PM||||Hey artherd:<P>Could you give us a hint.<P>Am I wrong in assuming this car is not domestic ?||||reg||3
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||10-01-2001||01:13 PM||||Any external mods you do usually constitute a compromise. Remove the cat and put on an air induction system , you loose low end torque.<P>There's no real way to gain large Amounts of HP without opening up the motor , adding a turbo , SC , or NOS.<P>JM ||||reg||1
